# The signed approvals, part `full-review-fixes-fronts`: the front ends'
# fixes of the full review. Written with the code.

# ------------------------------------------------ what the store names

[break] the-store-named-it-is-said-approved
rule: `permissions trust` says of an extension or a hook the trust store names at the hash shown that this is not checked, never that it was approved before: an entry the model wrote reads the same.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
in-string: The trust store names it at this hash
replace: Approved before at this hash
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_permissions_trust_approves_a_projects_extensions_on_a_signed_yes

[break] the-list-says-your-signature
rule: `permissions list` says an unchecked entry carries a signature, not the person's signature.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
in-string: its trust carries a signature
replace: its trust carries your signature
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_a_project_trusted_with_permissions_trust_is_trusted_on_the_next_start

# ------------------------------------------------ what `permissions trust` signs

[break] the-rules-are-shown-after-the-password
rule: `permissions trust` shows the project's rules and settings before the password, which signs them as shown.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
in: permissions
find: out!("{}", reading_text(&reading));
replace: let _ = reading_text(&reading);
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_a_project_trusted_with_permissions_trust_is_trusted_on_the_next_start

[break] a-reading-the-files-no-longer-hold-is-pinned
rule: The core pins the rules as the reading shown holds them, and refuses, writing nothing, when the project's files hold other rules or settings by the yes.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/manage.rs
in: Core::trust_project_with
find: if now.rules_pin.hash != reading.rules_pin.hash || now.settings != reading.settings {
replace: if false {
packages: cineris-core,cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it trusting::a_trust_is_refused_when_the_rules_changed_after_they_were_shown
    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_a_project_trusted_with_permissions_trust_is_trusted_on_the_next_start

# ------------------------------------------------ Ctrl+C at a headless run's password

[break] ctrl-c-at-a-runs-password-goes-on-without
rule: `Ctrl+C` at a headless run's password ends the run as interrupted (130), before its session opens; `Esc` goes on without the approvals.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in: read
find: None if terminal.interrupted() => Err(NotSigned::Interrupted)
replace: None if false => Err(NotSigned::Interrupted)
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system approvals::sys_a_headless_run_with_no_terminal_asks_nothing_and_says_why

[break] the-prompt-does-not-tell-ctrl-c-from-esc
rule: The terminal's password prompt tells `Ctrl+C` from `Esc`, so that a headless run can end on the first.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/secret/password.rs
in: ask_on
find: interrupted = true;
replace: interrupted = false;
packages: cineris-tui,cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-tui secret::password::tests::at_a_terminal_esc_and_ctrl_c_give_nothing
    cineris-cli::system approvals::sys_a_headless_run_with_no_terminal_asks_nothing_and_says_why

# ------------------------------------------------ the debugger's check

[break] traced-always-false
rule: `harden::traced` tells a process with a real tracer that it is traced.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/harden.rs
