# ------------------------------------------------ the terminal taken early

[break] the-application-takes-the-terminal-after-its-core
rule: The application takes the terminal before its core starts, so that a password typed early is not echoed.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/interactive.rs
in: run
find: app::TakenTerminal::enter(overrides).ok()
replace: app::TakenTerminal::enter(overrides).ok().filter(|_| false)
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system approvals::sys_a_password_typed_before_a_subcommand_or_a_run_asks_is_never_echoed

[break] the-question-takes-what-was-typed-before-it
rule: The yes or no before the password throws away what was typed while the terminal was taken, so that nothing typed before it answers it.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in: Taken::confirm
find: let _ = terminal.drain();
replace: let _ = &mut terminal;
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system approvals::sys_a_yes_typed_before_the_question_does_not_answer_it

[break] the-yes-line-is-not-wiped
rule: The line the yes or no is read from is written over once it is judged.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in: yes_of
find: forget_line(line);
replace: drop(line);
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris approvals::tests::a_yes_or_no_line_is_judged_and_written_over

# ------------------------------------------------ the shipped binary closed, the reset's words

[break] the-binary-does-not-close-itself
rule: The real binary closes its own process to the user's other programs, first thing in `main`.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/main.rs
in: main
find: let hardened = cineris_sandbox::harden::harden();
replace: let hardened = std::io::Result::Ok(());
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system hardened::sys_the_binary_closes_its_own_process*

[break] the-resets-warning-leaves-the-gates-out
rule: The reset's warning says that what each approval pinned keeps its gates until it is approved again.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in-string: hook they pinned keeps its gates
replace: hook they pinned lets its gates go
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris approvals::tests::the_resets_warning_says_what_keeps_its_gates
